/** @page soundfont_system SoundFont System Overview
 *  @brief Overview of SoundFont management in Maestro MPTK.
 *
 *  @details
 *  The SoundFont system defines the samples, banks, and presets used by
 *  the synthesizer to render MIDI playback.
 *
 *  SoundFonts can be:
 *  - provided by the internal MPTK database,
 *  - loaded from a local file,
 *  - downloaded dynamically from a remote server.
 *
 *  This system also exposes banks and presets so applications can:
 *  - build instrument-selection user interfaces,
 *  - inspect the structure of the active SoundFont,
 *  - prepare MIDI bank and preset changes.
 *
 *  @section soundfont_start Quick Start
 *
 *  @code
 *  midiSynth.MPTK_SoundFont.LoadedCallback = synth =>
 *  {
 *      Debug.Log($"SoundFont ready: {synth.MPTK_SoundFont.SoundFontName}");
 *  };
 *
 *  midiSynth.MPTK_SoundFont.Load("https://example.com/MySoundFont.sf2");
 *  @endcode
 *
 *  @section soundfont_pages Related Pages
 *
 *  Read these pages in the following order:
 *
 *  - @subpage soundfont_overview
 *  - @subpage soundfont_runtime_loading
 *  - @subpage soundfont_banks_presets
 *  - @subpage soundfont_best_practices
 *
 *  @section soundfont_modules Related Modules
 *
 *  - @ref audio_resources
 *  - @ref soundfont_management
 *  - @ref synth_engine
 *
 *  @section soundfont_next Next Steps
 *
 *  - @ref getting_started
 *  - @ref detailed_guides
 *  - @ref soundfont_management_hub
 */
